                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6c9aef9-9d70-4b31-bd7b-be6505c23561",
                                                "sense_id": "05558d74-b8d6-3643-a27d-bdc5a178da6f",
                                                "text": "Backfiring in mercury arc rectifiers has now been pinpointed as the primary cause of the Glasgow transformer failures. […] The chief causes of rectifier backfiring in the Glasgow units were overheating or unfavourable anode/cathode temperature differential; it has proved possible to overcome these, although occasional backfires do still occur."
                                            }
